    note for OrderStore "acceptOnce is one indivisible acceptance decision: same scoped attempt returns original acceptance before new-order checks, otherwise validates current hours/menu and records exactly one order with accepted lines. A failed decision creates no order. changeIfCurrent checks observed revision, lifecycle and reason and records order plus employee/time history together. Mechanisms belong to implementation."
    note for CheckoutService "Early validation is for useful corrections, not final acceptance authority. resolveRejectedAttempt checks whether a racing identical attempt was accepted before presenting rejection. Proposals never authorize unreviewed price/item changes."
    note for SubmissionIdentity "Logical identity of one customer's submission. Absence of an accepted record alone is not proof that an in-flight attempt was rejected. No UUID, session/cookie scheme, storage representation or lifetime is prescribed. Accepted identity cannot authorize a different selection or expose another customer's order."
    note for Order "Accepted contents and totals are immutable. Revision is an opaque observed-state marker, not a prescribed database field type. PrivateLink grants read access only to this order."
    note for UpdateCoordinator "Logical current-data responsibility. Polling, push, rendering strategy and scheduling are open. Preserve input and filter, record successful check only, retain stale data with warning and recover current information. Never automatically repeat a rejected or uncertain staff write."
    note for AccessService "All staff reads/writes require current authorized identity, including requests bypassing visible UI. Identity and credential handling may use framework-native facilities."
    note for Money "Exact monetary meaning, not a prescribed numeric storage representation. Other named types denote product values or collections, not extra mandatory runtime classes."
